ui_bugs.issue:
CRITICAL SYNTAX ERROR — stray leftover edit at end of file: 'nter",
    marginTop: 16,
  },
}));' caused Metro to fail with 'SyntaxError: Unterminated string constant. (1818:4)'. Entire Expo frontend returned HTTP 500 and NOTHING rendered (including the new SCHEDULED PAYMENTS section). FIXED by removing the four stray lines after the legitimate closing '}));' on line 1817.

rca_of_issue:
Frontend feature appeared totally broken (PaymentAccountsSection missing from DOM, dealer detail showed ACCOUNTS jumping straight to AGENTS) until I checked /var/log/supervisor/expo.out.log and found 'Metro error: SyntaxError: /app/frontend/app/(tabs)/index.tsx: Unterminated string constant. (1818:4)'. Lines 1818-1821 contained leftover garbage from a prior incomplete edit ('nter",
    marginTop: 16,
  },
}));') AFTER the legitimate end-of-file '}));' on line 1817. Because Metro bundles all routes in a single graph, ONE file's syntax error cascades — Expo serves HTTP 500 for everything, AND the previously-cached bundle (which predated the new PaymentAccountsSection JSX) was being served from the browser making it LOOK like only the new feature failed. Removing the 4 stray lines restored the bundle and the SCHEDULED PAYMENTS section appeared immediately.
